{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_2021688056#4_3321151831","relevance":3,"reason":"This is a dedicated segment of the Target loss prevention/shoplifting policy article and gives direct apprehension policy details: suspects are identified after concealing merchandise, security should seek cooperation before physical apprehension, officers may apprehend suspects inside or outside the store, preferably in pairs, then take them to an office and wait for police.","learned":"Target loss prevention/security officers reportedly may apprehend shoplifting suspects inside or outside the store, are advised to do so in pairs, and may hold/question them while awaiting police."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1254","reason":"The apprehension query is producing highly relevant policy details from an unjudged segment; continue to find the next segment or additional direct evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1254"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_2021688056#5_3321153488","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1254","rank":5,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_2021688056#5_3321153488\" , \"end_char\": 4186.000000 , \"headings\": \"Target Loss Prevention Policy: Fines, Legal Penalties, etc Target Loss Prevention Policy: Fines, Legal Penalties, etc Table of Contents Target Loss Prevention Policy General Target Loss Prevention Policy Suspect <cover>Apprehension Legal Penalties: Target Shoplifting </cover>Fines and More Other Store Shoplifting Policies \" , \"segment\": \"After apprehending a suspect, the loss prevention officers may take the suspect to their office to question them and await the arrival of police. Suspects are not required to speak to store officers. Target will have law enforcement proceed with an arrest if stolen merchandise is found on their person. Specific laws regarding apprehension and detention of larceny suspects may vary slightly by state. Legal Penalties: Target Shoplifting Fines and More Each state has guidelines that define a specific dollar amount as the criteria for determining whether a shoplifting offense is a misdemeanor or a felony. For example, New York law states that a theft totaling under $1,000 is classified as a misdemeanor. A theft over $1,000 qualifies as ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_2021688056#0_3321144158","rank":3,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_2021688056#1_3321145933","rank":4,"relevance":3}]}}
{"request":{"judgments":"6/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_2021688056#5_3321153488","relevance":3,"reason":"This dedicated Target loss prevention/shoplifting policy segment directly states post-apprehension procedures: loss prevention may take suspects to an office, suspects need not speak to store officers, Target will have law enforcement proceed with arrest if stolen merchandise is found, and penalties vary by state and dollar amount.","learned":"After apprehension, Target loss prevention may detain/question suspects while awaiting police; Target reportedly seeks arrest through law enforcement if stolen merchandise is found."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ target shoplifting arrest stolen merchandise)","reason":"Search for additional Target-specific pages or segments discussing arrest/prosecution after shoplifting, using concrete terms from the strongest evidence while avoiding exact duplicate policy phrasing."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ target shoplifting arrest stolen merchandise)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_2016099027#4_3306908806","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1255","rank":3,"snippet":"shelving. CVS also monitors for theft by employees. Store managers and asset protection staff conduct cash verifications, employee bag checks, and investigations of potential internal thefts. Suspect Apprehension Asset protection coordinators do not apprehend suspects, according to the official job description and CVS’ recruiting department. For the safety of its employees and customers, CVS prohibits employees from physically confronting or chasing those suspected of shoplifting. They can, however, follow and/or approach suspects inside the store. The store manager has the final say on how to proceed with a <cover>shoplifting suspect. Arrest and Prosecution If you are caught stealing from CVS and the store manager decides to contact local law enforcement, officials will follow state guidelines regarding theft. Our article on asset protection at Target has more information about theft laws, fines, and jail time. Potential charges include misdemeanor or felony larceny (depending on the value of the stolen merchandise) </cover>and possession of stolen property.\" , \"start_char\": 2555.000000 , \"title\": \"CVS Shoplifting Policy Explained in Detail: Know What Would Happen - First Quarter Finance\" , \"url\": \"https://firstquarterfinance.com/cvs-shoplifting-policy/\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_2021688056#5_3321153488","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_2016099027#5_3306910580","rank":2,"relevance":1}]}}
