{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1317"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_437976670#1_919396346","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1317","rank":7,"snippet":"phone records produced a photo with the supplier standing next to the former target. Clearview AI provided a potential identity, which was later confirmed. Multiple agencies across the country had investigative interest in the same <cover>target and this identification allowed for crucial inter-agency coordination. Texas Constable’s Office Gets Leads in Cases Where None Previously Existed A Montgomery County Texas Constable’s Office had numerous cases with no leads, including cases of robbery, shoplifting, online solicitation of a minor, home invasions, and a fraud investigation where a suspect stole the identities of 17 individuals. The agency stated that Clearview AI helped provide them unique, invaluable leads for these cases, which were followed up with more traditional investigative techniques. INTERVIEWS MEDIA HIGHLIGHTS TIME100 Most Influential Companies Your Face Is Not Your Own IN THE NEWS INTERESTED IN a PILOT? \" , \"segment\": \"Investigative & Major Crimes Units Counter-terrorism Units Conservation & Preservation Services Intelligence & Crime Analysis Units Patrol & Security Operations Law Enforcement</cover>Background Checks Learn More CUSTOMER SPOTLIGHTS Georgia Police Department Lends a Hand to Fellow Agency to Help Solve Mail Theft Case As mail theft continues to adversely impact the Atlanta area, agencies like the Georgia ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_2016099027#5_3306910580","rank":5,"relevance":1},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_2016099027#4_3306908806","rank":6,"relevance":1}]}}
