{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_280206102#5_686412301","relevance":2,"reason":"This Business Insider article is about Target store secrets, not dedicated to Target's shoplifting policy. However, it contains direct supporting evidence from a Target employee claiming Target stores often let shoplifters go until the stolen amount reaches a felony threshold, along with comments about strong surveillance.","learned":"Independent anecdotal support: a Target employee reportedly told Business Insider that stores may let shoplifters continue until the theft amount qualifies as a felony, and Target is known for strong camera surveillance."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1323","reason":"The felony/shoplifters query surfaced a new Target-specific source with direct supporting evidence; continue to see whether more results discuss Target's shoplifting prosecution or felony-threshold practices."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1323"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_280206102#6_686414962","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1323","rank":2,"snippet":"big box store SEE ALSO: Costco employees explain why they don't buy produce there \" , \"segment\": \"\\\"I worked at Target in the early nineties and it was insane then,\\\" another Reddit user added. \\\" Twenty years later and I wouldn't be surprised if they weigh me as I enter and as I leave to determine if I'm shoplifting.\\\" One Target employee told Business Insider that the surveillance system doesn't ensure that all shoplifters get busted immediately, however. \\\"Stores will often let <cover>shoplifters go until they steal an amount that will be counted as a felony — sending them straight to jail,\" the Target </cover>employee told Business Insider. Be nice to employees — it might pay off. AP Photo/Damian Dovarganes Sometimes, it pays to be nice. Business Insider's Kate Taylor previously reported on a viral blog started by Target employee Tom Grennell. He wrote about working during a special sale when his Target store was giving out a 10% discount on all purchases. The store had mailed out a coupon, but if customers forgot their copies, they could ask for another coupon. \"I have a coupon to scan if anyone asks for it."}}
